{
  "_doc": "Shared scoring fixtures. Both scorers read this one file: Kotlin from\nScoringFixtureParityTest (off the jvmTest classpath) and JavaScript from\nfunctions/assessment-scoring.test.js (by relative path). A new case belongs here and\nnowhere else — neither suite needs a code edit to pick one up.\n\n'content' and 'answer' are decoded straight into QuestionContent and UserAnswer, so they\nmust satisfy those classes' init-block invariants and carry both discriminators under\n'type': PascalCase for content (SingleChoice, MultipleChoice, Ordering, FillBlank, Survey)\nand kebab-case for answers (single-choice, multiple-choice, ordering, fill-blank, survey).\n'imageUrl' has no default and must be written out, null included.\n\n'expected' is the score digit (evaluateAnswer, 1..9), the percent (computePercentScore,\n0..100) or the star tenths (computeStars, 0..30).\n\n'kotlinRejectsCodeAnswer' marks a raw string the CodeAnswer value class refuses to hold\n(CodeAnswer.kt:11 requires a non-empty string). The server has no such wrapper and still\nhas to answer, so JavaScript asserts 'expected' while Kotlin asserts the rejection.\n\nCases marked FLAGGED mirror Kotlin behaviour that looks like a bug. They are pinned here\ndeliberately: fix the Kotlin, and this file changes with it — on both sides at once.",
